  "version": "0.5.5-beta.4",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.5.5-beta.3`\n\n### Fixes\n\n- play the notification sound on Linux when it is asked for, through notify-send's sound-name hint, since the request's sound flag was ignored there and Rust 1.99 flags it as never read ([79bbc97a](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/79bbc97a35a9fe15535c3505872fe0a2fb91fbe2))\n- write Codex's Windows hook command without quotes, since Codex hands it to cmd /C as one Rust-quoted argument where each quote arrives as \\\\\" and cmd failed every hook looking for a program named \\\\\"C:\\\\...; a path with spaces goes in by its short name ([77fddf23](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/77fddf232a7494d1aa62e46e58190f1fb927c6bf))\n\n### UI and usability\n\n- tuck the title bar's settings buttons 10px under the native window buttons, since the wide padding around the native glyphs left the two groups looking far apart ([11b28275](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/11b28275e25d2e515434e42bd531da898620a899))\n- make the native Windows window buttons 36px tall like the title bar, since at 32px they centred 2px above the app's own buttons and their hover left a strip uncovered ([cdc80892](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/cdc808928db44c424158cf559f8a57509ba1f852))\n\n### Other changes\n\n- rewrite two descending sorts with sort_by_key, a fallthrough with ?, and a nested if as a match guard, since the clippy in Rust 1.99 rejects the old forms and CI runs the latest stable ([5244d5eb](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/5244d5ebfb05654a717a6e36fbe82ad58455d35a))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.5.5-beta.3...v0.5.5-beta.4](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.5.5-beta.3...v0.5.5-beta.4)",
